<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales off 0.3 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales off 0.3 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales fell 0.3 percent in the week ended March 1 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 6.7 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index was up 2.0 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales were generally on-to-above plan for most retailers,&quot; the report said. &quot;In the latest period, the weekly sales index slipped below its rolling 16-week trend following two above-trend readings,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>(( --N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
